    "graphrag": {
      "answer": "Female customer opinion points form an elongated continuous curved band across the ternary domain, extending from higher Negative values through moderate Uncertainty toward Positive values. [G6] [G35] Male customer opinion points form an elongated band-like arrangement spanning the Negative–Uncertainty and Uncertainty–Positive legs of the ternary plot. [G7] [G36] Overall, the Female and Male categories have a similar band-like cluster structure running from higher Negative values through moderate Uncertainty toward higher Positive values. [G24] [G33] In the radial stacked bar view, the greatest visible Female segment is in the upper-right Positive opinion sector and has a radial height of 93.9 px. [G4] For Male customers, the maximum visible customer-count bar has a radial height of 79.9 px. [G3]",
